cals_dz","deck_planks","door_planks","glass_dirty","mud","plaster_rough","signs","steel_galv","timber_beam","timber_grey","timber_siding","timber_tarred","wood_paint"],"theater":"desert","snow":false,"nodes":["main","door_engine-1","door_engine1","decals","door_doghouse"],"vertex_colors":"COLOR_0 ubyte (grime x base colour; alpha = decal opacity)","revision":"desert rework 2 (2026-09-26)","rework":{"asset":"every derrick member is angle iron (L profile) with its own UVs (no smearing), gusset plates with bolts at every joint, crown block with visible sheaves, gin pole, racking board with fingers and racked pipe stands, four guy lines to deadmen; painted red-oxide (no black); detailed drawworks (frames, drum with wraps, brake rims, chain guard, levers), engine inside the house, 24-pipe rack, pit walkway and mud lines","common":"new desert lib materials with real albedo breakup (limewash_worn, mud_render, mudbrick, sandstone_ochre, screed_roof, bitumen_felt, corrugated_galv, patio_flags, palm_log, canvas_camo, darj_panel); decal atlas feathered (no hard quads); interior_dark cards replaced by dim plaster / modelled interiors; AO atlas background dilated (no black mip bleed); warm sand-bounce vertex tint on sun-averted faces; KHR_mesh_quantization (normals/tangents int8, uv1 u16); effective-albedo floor (material lum >= 0.045 linear, material x vertex-colour >= 0.03) and opacity caps on near-black decals (soot 0.5, crack 0.7) so iron, tar, char, scorch and crude never render as pure-black voids; LOD2 re-tuned to ~12-15% of LOD0"},"rework2":{"asset":"LOD2 tank keeps its cylinder (size-aware LOD floor); racked drill pipe as thin paired stands; spill decals soft.","common":"LOD1/LOD2 rebuilt with a shape-preserving per-part reducer (lodfix.py): planar dissolve per part delimited by material, UV seams and vertex-colour bands; only curved parts are collapse-decimated, each on its own with a size-aware floor; no joined-mesh collapse, so walls, courtyards, minaret shafts and tanks keep their shape (no holes, sliver fans or UV smears). LOD2 drops sub-pixel parts (wire, ladders, rope). Weathering decals use a soft desert atlas (decals_dz: 2 variants per kind, random mirror, feathered, no hard quads); roof patches are soft stains plus one feathered relief repair; render loss shows rubble (never orange brick) with a 3.5 cm broken edge. New shared CC0 materials: mud_render2 (Poly Haven dirt_floor, darker/redder than the sand, 2x the fine detail), screed_lime (grey_plaster_02, no craze pattern), limewash_lumpy (medieval_wall_01), corrugated_zinc (corrugated_iron_02), palm_frond_dz (alpha-tested frond / reed-mat atlas, own work). Stronger warm ground bounce in shade (limewash no longer turns blue). Water jars are lathe-turned buff clay (belly, neck, lugs); sandbags are individual pillow bags (squash, sag, pinched tied ends, random bond); sand drifts are low wind ramps feathering into the ground; debris mounds have a soft toe (no rim)."},"gltf_extensions_required":["KHR_mesh_quantization"],"group":"desert"}